  "authoring": {
    "note": "The island line's own platforms, beyond the barrier. The trains are visibly smaller — narrower gauge, four short carriages, no first class — and run to a timetable that is not published outside the Transfer. Standing room only at shift change. The seaward side is fenced along its entire length; the posted notice calls it a safety measure.",
